body:
Why can't we simply detect whether we're in a node environment? The functionality we're talking about is inside `getBuiltinModules` which, by the way, already falls back to a hard coded list of modules for older versions of Node.JS.

I believe all we have to do is check for node's global `process` variable (or some more reliable way of detecting our execution environment):

```
var node_env = typeof process !== 'undefined'; // or preferably something smarter ;)
if (!node_env) {
    return [];
} else if (process.version.match(/^v0\.[0-7]\./) {
    // return hard coded list of modules for node version < 0.8 (already available in the rule)
} else {
    return require("repl")._builtinLibs;
}
```
